<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iwaz Khalji</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1227</span> · Also known as Ghiyath al-Din Iwaz Khalji</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iwaz Khalji, who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Ghiyath al-Din from about 1212 to 1227, was the most capable ruler of the Khalji dynasty of Bengal. He built roads and embankments, created a river fleet and struck coins in his own name. He was defeated and killed by forces sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iltutmish">Iltutmish</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iwaz-khalji.jpg" alt="Iwaz Khalji" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Islamic_Sultanates._Bengal._Ghiyath_al-Din_%27Iwad._Governor,_AH_614-616_AD_1217-1220._Struck_in_the_name_of_Shams_al-Din_Iltutmish,_Sultan_of_Dehli.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
